    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d104">

                <pb facs="0198" n="178" sameAs="frus:frus1950v07/pg178"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 Muccio, John J.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Acting Political Adviser in Japan</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Sebald</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">unclassified</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                        
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-06-26T21:00:00-04:00">June 26, 1950—9 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>483. For Ambassador.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d104-f1"/> While Department deeply
                    appreciates willingness you and members your staff remain Seoul, it is felt
                    inadvisable for you or any members your staff voluntarily to become hostages and
                    accordingly unless there are overriding considerations not known here Department
                    feels you should endeavor leave Seoul to join Goverment before safe departure
                    becomes impossible.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d104-f1" n="1" xml:id="d104-f1-content">
                <p>This message was repeated to Seoul as Department telegram 629.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
